+# Manual NIFTY option protection: diagnosis and change
+
+Your NIFTY 13-Oct-2026 22250 PE was not registered as a managed KADIMA position, so the exit monitor had no position to protect. The 9 October log repeatedly records an unresolved SELL for a different, older SENSEX position; the original reconciliation code returned before fetching broker positions or performing manual adoption whenever that ledger refresh failed. Even if reconciliation had succeeded, the original adoption code deliberately observed valid CARRYFORWARD longs without creating a Position. The records do not contain your manual buy's product type, quantity, price or classification, so the carryforward explanation is conditional. The 15:15–15:40 window is not the demonstrated cause, and no relationship to the kill latch can be established.
+
+## Evidence (all times IST)
+
+The on-disk instrument cache identifies `NIFTY13OCT2622250PE` as token `44597`, lot size 65. Instrument identifiers here are public contract identifiers, not authentication tokens.
+
+| Source | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `/var/lib/kadima/audit/2026-10-09.jsonl` | Zero exact contract/token events. There is no recorded manual BUY, product type, quantity, buy average, adoption reason or stop evaluation for this contract. A broad numeric `22250` match was an unrelated SHIELD_SCORE value and was excluded. |
+| `positions` | No row for the symbol or contract token, including closed history. Consequently `check_exits` could not select a Position for this holding. |
+| `trade_audit_plans` | One **8 October**, not 9 October, SCALP suggestion: 14:46:34.708768, score 84.43, proposed entry 146.10, stage SETUP_READY, blocker fresh_news_coverage_required. This is a suggestion, not proof of your manual execution. |
+| `oi_snapshots`, 9 October | 510 stored samples; first 09:15:39.723260 at ₹86.30; last 15:39:36.556972 at ₹23.80; daily range ₹22.85–₹95.00. First-to-last sampled fall about 72.4%, **not** a measured return from your unknown buy price. |
